6fe7c","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch5_augmented_matrix_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is preserved when an elementary row operation is applied to an augmented matrix?","options":["The number of unknowns only if the row operation is a swap.","The exact coefficient matrix.","The individual entries of the matrix.","The solution set of the represented system."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a1888ad880953153480abecb","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch5_augmented_matrix_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"An augmented matrix has size $4\\times6$ for a system with $4$ equations. How many unknowns are there?","options":["$4$","$2$","$6$","$5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0fd83a678c2b12ef5e60b45b","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch5_augmented_matrix_017","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A reduced augmented matrix has a row $(0\\ 0\\ \\cdots\\ 0\\mid c)$ with $c\\ne0$. What does this imply about the corresponding linear system?","options":["has a unique solution","has a free variable","is inconsistent (has no solution)","has infinitely many solutions"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bfce48fd54469b93852d66ef","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch5_augmented_matrix_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why do row operations have to be applied across the entire augmented row, including the right-hand side?","options":["The right-hand side column is not part of the system.","Only coefficient entries may be changed during elimination.","The last column must stay fixed in every equivalent system.","Each row represents a whole equation, including its constant term."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a04a60804a62750548542efc","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch5_augmented_matrix_008_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which augmented matrix represents the system $x_1+2x_3=5$, $x_2-x_3=1$ in the unknowns $x_1,x_2,x_3$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}1&0&2&5\\\\0&1&-1&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&5\\\\1&-1&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&0&5\\\\1&-1&0&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&0&2&5\\\\0&1&1&1\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f765709b05413138784805f9","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch5_augmented_matrix_019_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"After $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-2R_1$ is applied to the augmented matrix $\\begin{pmatrix}1&1&2\\\\2&3&5\\end{pmatrix}$, what is the new second row?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&3\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1&5\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2&3&1\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4147ffb0816a75b1e8568461","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_math_ii_linear_algebra_augmented_matrix_98558f4e_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which augmented matrix, with columns in the order $x$, $y$, right-hand side, represents the system $x+2y=5$, $3x=y+1$ in the unknowns $x,y$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&5\\\\3&1&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&5\\\\3&0&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&5\\\\-1&3&1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&5\\\\3&-1&1\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f951364773c56d04afc0f163","time_limit":30}]}}